Use this when measuring a team's Vercel AI Gateway spend, request volume, token usage, or latency. Returns totals for the chosen metrics, optionally grouped by one dimension such as model or provider, plus an hourly or daily series when granularity is set. Covers the last 7 days by default. A scoped connection fixes the team/project; otherwise, pass projectId to limit the team query to one project. Returns aggregates only, never prompts or responses; use get_ai_gateway_leaderboard for usage across all of AI Gateway.

```ts
mcp__Vercel__get_ai_gateway_usage(args: {
// Also return a time series with this bucket size. The window can span at most 100 buckets. For hour, specify a window of at most 100 hours (e.g. since: "24h"); use day for the default 7-day window. The window is widened to whole UTC buckets, and the returned start and end show the widened window.
granularity?: "hour" | "day",
// Break the totals down by this dimension.
groupBy?: "aiModel" | "aiProvider" | "aiModelType" | "projectId" | "environment" | "httpStatus" | "isByok",
// Maximum groups to return. Defaults to 10.
limit?: integer, // minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Metrics to return. Defaults to cost and count. cost is billed spend in USD, count is requests, the token metrics are sums, and the two _ms metrics are averages. Groups are ranked by the first metric.
metrics?: Array<"cost" | "count" | "input_tokens" | "output_tokens" | "time_to_first_token_ms" | "request_duration_ms">, // minItems: 1
// Only usage from this project. Omit for the whole team only when the connection is not already scoped to a project.
// The ID or slug of the project.
// Project IDs start with "prj_".
// If you do not know the project ID or slug, it can be found through these mechanism:
// - Read the file .vercel/project.json if it exists and extract the projectId
// - Use the `list_projects` tool
projectId?: string,
// Start of the window as an ISO date or relative lookback from now (e.g. "24h", "7d"). Defaults to 7 days before until.
since?: string,
// The team ID (team_...) for team-wide usage. A team slug is supported only together with projectId. Use list_teams to discover an unknown team ID.
teamId: string,
// Optional end of the window as an ISO date, relative lookback, or "now". Omit this when the end should be the current time.
until?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

